<title>SWEDEN: Sandvik shares rise on buy back rumours.</title>
<headline>Sandvik shares rise on buy back rumours.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Swedish specialty metals and toolmaker Sandvik climbed on Thursday on a rumour the company was planning to buy back some of its own shares.</p>
<p>At 1445 the share traded up 8.5 crowns at 180.5 in lively turnover as other engineering sector shares made smaller gains.</p>
<p>&quot;There is speculation the company is going to buy back shares. The same rumour made (Swedish steel company) SSAB rise 10 crowns a while back,&quot; one analyst said.</p>
<p>Others said rumours of an official listing in the U.S. were fuelling the increase.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1011</p>
</text>
